        "original_id": "c493c351-9f86-5eba-aa77-38e759f36000",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dick Crealy, Mary Pierce, Larisa Neiland, Peaches Bartkowicz\n- Events: Australian Open, 1970 Australian Davis Cup Team, 1970 Swedish Open, 2000 Sparkassen Cup – Doubles, Olympics\n- Organizations: Women's Tennis Association\n\nFacts:\n- Richard Crealy was born on 18 September 1944 and is an Australian former tennis player.\n- In 1970, Dick Crealy reached the finals of the Australian Open and was a member of the 1970 Australian Davis Cup Team.\n- In 1970, Dick Crealy won the men's singles title at the Swedish Open, and Peaches Bartkowicz won the women's singles title.\n- Dick Crealy won four Grand Slam titles in doubles.\n- Mary Pierce was born on 15 January 1975 and is a French retired tennis professional who played on the Women's Tennis Association tour.\n- Mary Pierce represented France in team competitions and at the Olympics.\n- Mary Pierce and Larisa Neiland were the defending champions for the 2000 Sparkassen Cup – Doubles, but neither competed that year.",
